    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d570">

                <pb facs="0737" n="726" sameAs="frus:frus1937v02/pg726"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123En3/568: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Iran</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Teheran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-17T12:00:00+03:25">November 17,
                        1937—noon.</date><lb/>[Received 2:11 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>109. My despatch No. 1118, August 28.<anchor n="12" xml:id="d570-f1"/> Foreign
                    Minister returned last week and received me this morning.</p>
                <p>He volunteered the information that he was about to recommend to the Shah that
                    their Legation in Washington be reopened in the near future. He said he would
                    tell me more about it by the end of the month as His Majesty was at present in
                    Resht.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
